<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan electronics up on sound 1997 outlook.</title>
<headline>Taiwan electronics up on sound 1997 outlook.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's electronics shares surged in late Thursday trade on forecasts of a positive outlook in 1997, brokers said.</p>
<p>Brokers also attributed the electronics' gains partly to a reaction to U.S. computer share IBM's overnight rise.</p>
<p>With 45 minutes left, electronics rose 2.99 percent while the overall index was up 1.36 percent.</p>
<p>Acer surged T$2 or 3.96 percent to T$52.5 and ASE rose by the daily seven percent limit to T$67.  </p>
<p>&quot;Most leading electronic shares are expected to enjoy some 40-50 percent profit growth in 1997,&quot; said Nikko Securities research chief Michael Hung.</p>
<p>&quot;No doubt, electronics will be one of the market's bellwether shares this year,&quot; Hung said.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
